{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.not_forall_frobenius_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.not_forall_frobenius_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicGaloisCharacter.lean#L93-L111","doc":"**The class is not vacuous.**  No `MotivicGaloisCharacter` has an\nidentically-zero Frobenius family.\n\nThis is the point of `frobenius_realize_ne_zero`.  The substrate axiom\n`nonarchimedean_nontrivial` supplies a finite place with a nontrivial\ntarget; realization is a ring hom, so it sends `0` to `0`; and the\ncompatibility law forbids that.  Before the law was added, the\nall-zero family was a legitimate instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_realize_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_realize_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicGaloisCharacter.lean#L89-L89","doc":"**Realization-tower compatibility.**\n\nAt every finite place whose realization target is nontrivial, the\nlocal Frobenius character is *visible in the tower*: its image\nunder the substrate's realization map at that place is nonzero.\n\nThis is the law the class docstring has always promised and never\nencoded.  Without it the class carries a single data field and no\nProp field at all, so `⟨fun _ => 0⟩` inhabits it and every\ndownstream `[MotivicGaloisCharacter …]` hypothesis is discharged by\na character that is identically zero — see\n`not_forall_frobenius_eq_zero` below, which is exactly the\nstatement this field buys.\n\n**Scope — what this does NOT encode.**  The full compatibility of\n`χ^mot_{A,p}` with the realization tower would relate\n`frobenius_at p` to a Frobenius *operator* on `Target\n(Place.finite p)` and to `motiveA` through it.  `MotivicSubstrate`\nsupplies no such operator, so that statement is not expressible\nhere.  What is encoded is the non-degeneracy half: the character\ndoes not vanish where the tower is non-degenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_at","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicGaloisCharacter.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Local Frobenius eigenvalue at a finite prime `p`,\nrepresented as an element of the dimension-completion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicGaloisCharacter.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","kind":"class","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicGaloisCharacter.lean#L31-L91","doc":"**Motivic Galois character of a Frobenius–Hopf substrate.**\n\nAxiomatic class encoding the cyclotomic-Galois action on the\nmotivic class `[A]` of the substrate.  Parameters:\n* `K0 Mhat` — Grothendieck ring + dimension-completion\n  ([`MotivicSubstrate`](MotivicSubstrate)).\n* `Target` — realisation target functor (passed through to\n  `MotivicSubstrate`).\n* `motiveA : Mhat` — the motivic class of the substrate $A$.\n\nThe class **takes a `MotivicSubstrate` instance as a\nhypothesis** (per `def:motivic-galois-character` narrative),\nmaking the Galois character genuinely local to a substrate\nrather than free-floating type parameters.\n\nFields encode the family of local Frobenius characters\n$\\chi^{\\mathrm{mot}}_{A, p}$ at each finite place, satisfying\na compatibility with the realization tower of the substrate.\n\n**Architectural note (2026-08-12):** the `almost_everywhere_nontrivial`\nfield was removed from this class.  The perpetual obstruction is now\na standalone theorem (`perpetual_obstruction_from_collapse_invariant`\nin `MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean`) proved via the\nprime-ideal-collapse argument: C = a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1), with |C| > 1\nfor all QOU atoms.  Encoding it as a class field forced every\ninstance to either prove it or launder an axiom — the Route A proof\nshows it is a *consequence* of the Habiro structure, not an input.\n\nRef: [yekutieli2010], [tate1967]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:motivic-galois-character","label":"def:motivic-galois-character","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-galois-character.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}